# Social Sharing Assets

## Folder structure

All OG images live in `public/og/`. Never put social sharing images anywhere else.
Each route gets its own subfolder. The image inside is always named `og.png`.

```
public/
  og/
    default.png        ← site-wide fallback (Layout.astro)
    fitness/
      og.png           ← /fitness route
    contact/
      og.png           ← /contact route
```

## Naming convention

Create a subfolder named after the route slug and put `og.png` inside it.
`/fitness` → `fitness/og.png`. Nested routes mirror the URL path: `/services/chatbot` → `services/chatbot/og.png`.

## Image spec

- **Dimensions:** 1200 × 630 px (required — WhatsApp, Facebook, LinkedIn all expect this)
- **Format:** JPEG preferred for photos; PNG only for hard-edged graphics/logos
- **Size: under 300 KB** — WhatsApp's crawler silently skips previews for larger files
- **Safe zone:** keep text/logos within 960 × 504 px centered

## Layout props

Both `Layout.astro` and `FitnessLayout.astro` accept:

| Prop | Type | Default | What it controls |
|---|---|---|---|
| `title` | `string` | Site/page default | `<title>`, `og:title`, `twitter:title` |
| `description` | `string` | i18n site description | `og:description`, `twitter:description`, `<meta name="description">` |
| `ogImage` | `string` | `/og/default.png` | `og:image`, `twitter:image` |

Always pass all three when creating a new route.

## Rules

1. **NEVER hardcode a social image path** inside a layout default. The default must always point to `public/og/default.png` or `public/og/<route>.png`.
2. **NEVER use a page hero image** as the OG image. Hero images are not sized correctly (not 1200 × 630) and are typically multi-MB files that will break WhatsApp previews.
3. **Always use absolute URLs** for `og:image`. Both layouts handle this automatically via `new URL(ogImage, Astro.site)` — do not bypass this logic.
4. **Update CLAUDE.md** whenever you add a new OG image (the routes table in "Social Sharing / OG Images").
5. **Update `public/og/README.md`** to add the new route/file to the table.

## Adding a new route — checklist

- [ ] Create `public/og/<slug>/og.png` at 1200 × 630 px
- [ ] Pass `ogImage="/og/<slug>/og.png"` to the layout in the page file
- [ ] Pass a meaningful `description` (150–160 characters) — this is what appears in WhatsApp/iMessage previews
- [ ] Update the table in `CLAUDE.md` → Social Sharing section
- [ ] Update the table in `public/og/README.md`
